    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0268" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1309.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires at
                        London.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d177-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-23T22:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1913—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department understands that the present halt in China loan negotiations is
                    due to renewed discussion between Great Britain and Germany regarding adviser
                    for salt gabelle. Ascertain and report promptly views of Foreign Office as to
                    prospects early signature of loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d177-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d177-f1-content">
                <p>Same to American Embassy, Berlin.</p>
